Interesting Use Cases:
1) Personalized Care: Take measurments of patients body so our model can reflect them closer. This can get as in depth or as shallow as you need. Having measurments of each major part of limbs and anatomy would be important as not each human has same proportions. Taking basic vitals of the patient during specific movements can give us an insight to the workings of other systems during these movements and make for a more robust twin. Though this would require a model which can take in and account for a more wholistic view of our body and not just the muscoskeletal system. Video of patient movements can also be beneficial if our model can be trained to replicate their exact movements to give an insight to the potential issues within the system that could output that movement. 

2) Studying for Students: Getting real time feedback for different cases of muscle/skeletal issues and their impact not just on certain movements but getting data on how it impacts the other structures within the system. 

3) Treatment Plans: With a close twin of the patient it will allow us the test different treatment plans and see potential benefits or issues that may result from different approaches.  
